        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woven silk brocaded with silk and metal thread\nDisplayed behind glass.\nDark blue silk warp; dark blue silk ground weft.\nBrocading wefts: green, pink and orange silk and silver strip S-wound on a white silk core.\nSelvedge: one cord of plied white silk.\nDark blue ground with an unpatterned area at the bottom and then rows of a repeated motif: a bird with a large crest sitting on a short branch with a flower near the base and buds on top.  There is a butterfly by the buds.  There are 2 small cloud-like motifs between the birds on their branches.  The birds alternate direction in alternate rows."@en ;
